     1                                  ; E6 c18E (day2 round 2, agent E6, base DET2 rev2): live anchors FF 18 = call far [bx+si] (SI = 0 during dwell)
     2                                  ; instead of FF 1F; the E1 decoy block becomes 64 x FF 18 CC CC at 0FF80h..007Fh (absorbs the FF18CCCC backward
     3                                  ; searches from 0FFFFh of EmoMutants2 / segment_fault). Worker template, B/zombie FF 1F CC CC decoys unchanged, so
     4                                  ; FF1FCCCC searchers (2B2Team, OpcodeHunter1, ADDvanced, PastRAMa, ATO1, JMP2HELL2) only find dead decoys.
     5                                  ; Idea from night A015/c18 (screen 12ks2) and the zchain4 lineage (FF 18 anchors + FF 18 decoy at 0FF90h).
     6                                  ; D4 DET2: DET with B's [5D13h]/[0CC13h] writes back at instr 4/5 (rev1 rounds). DET's instr-3 [0CC13h]
     7                                  ; write tied with the zchain/zrl03/ah02 A write (instr 3) and lost the p0f13 hook half the time (screen n6sgd).
     8                                  ; D4 DET (day2, base rev1 KPHL): adaptive whole-team lattice. If a V6-family team is present (its B writes
     9                                  ; [4A17h] at instr 3; no other team in our fields writes that cell), every stream of ours (A, B, captured zombies)
    10                                  ; uses FAR_SEG 0FFAh = lattice 42h (10h below the V6-family 52h lattice, measured +0.28/+0.24 on leader2/3 cohorts
    11                                  ; in D4 W42 screen 0b3hc); otherwise FAR_SEG 0FFBh = 52h as in rev1 (W42's plain 2025/strong cost avoided).
    12                                  ; Detection: our B now writes [4A17h] late (instr 7), so at A's instr 5 and B's instr 5 the cell is still CCCCh
    13                                  ; unless a V6-family B wrote it at instr 3. A keeps the bit in BP; B patches the low byte of its own phoenix
    14                                  ; 'or dx,0FFBh' immediate (dec -> 0FAh) before any captured zombie can reach phoenix_init.
    15                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); DET edits by agent2 day2 role D4.
    16                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
    17                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
    18                                  bits 16
    19                                  
    20                                  ; B092 KL (warrior A): A031 K (E1 INT86 decoy block + A022 SD template edits) combined with the
    21                                  ; domain-2 defense A038 locpatA (B082 location start DI = 15*[1243h] + A038 window F2 81 C3 E1 -> FF 26 17 4A).
    22                                  ; Provenance: Good_Test V6 warrior 1 is friend-provided code (reconstructed source in
    23                                  ; study-notes/good-test-v6/source/); V6nohunt = agent2 edit (removed [7A00h] patch); E1/SD/locA2/locpatA are
    24                                  ; agent2 night edits (A031, A022, B082, A038); this merge = agent2 night role B092.
    25                                  ; Turn budget: locpatA startup (INT87 at instr 11) + E1 block (4 instr) + band math with a memory divisor
    26                                  ; (div/mul word [kq] instead of mov cx,3C00h; div cx; mul cx: same AX, one instruction fewer) + add si;
    27                                  ; phoenix_init still starts at turn 22 (as in rev0, K and locpatA). Data moved to the end (no jmp needed).
    28                                  ; B = A031 K_B (A026 Z1 + SD) unchanged.
